# Vowe — local configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you have. Every value is optional: Vowe
# degrades around each missing one rather than requiring it.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Never commit real keys.


# ── Models ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drives interpretation, observation (the L1 notes), and delegated answers.
# Without any key, Vowe still discovers sessions, ingests events, builds windows
# and shows deterministic status — notes just say nothing interpreted them.

# First-party Anthropic:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ...or any gateway that speaks the Anthropic message protocol:
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# VOWE_LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
# VOWE_LLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5

# Latency vs capability. Observation is the hot path — one call per window,
# continuously — so the defaults favour speed: claude-sonnet-5 at low effort.
# Raise either when capability matters more than the wait.
# VOWE_LLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5
# VOWE_LLM_EFFORT=low          # low | medium | high


# ── Vo's voice ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this, everything works except talking to Vo, and the UI says so.
# Observation does not depend on voice.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...
# VOWE_LIVE_MODEL=gpt-live-1
# VOWE_LIVE_VOICE=marin


# ── Structured decisions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for three things: which older window is relevant, whether a window
# justifies exploring, and how a development matches your stated preference.
# Without a key, each falls back to something deterministic.

# First-party TypeSafe:
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=...

# ...or through OpenRouter's decisions endpoint:
# VOWE_JEV_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/alpha/decisions
# VOWE_JEV_MODEL=typesafe/jev-1.13

# Ask, record what came back, but don't act on it — for comparing the decision
# model against the deterministic behaviour on real traffic before trusting it.
# VOWE_JEV_SHADOW=1


# ── Code knowledge ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vowe can keep a structural graph of each Project's repository, so that
# `search_context` over the repo returns architecture rather than only text
# matches. It is built by Graphify, a separate Python tool that Vowe detects but
# never installs:
#
#   uv tool install graphifyy
#
# Extraction runs locally from the AST and needs no API key. Without Graphify,
# repository search is `git grep` exactly as before, and the Project room says
# code knowledge is unavailable.

# VOWE_GRAPHIFY_BIN=/opt/homebrew/bin/graphify   # default: `graphify` on PATH
# VOWE_GRAPHIFY_MIN_VERSION=0.9.64               # refuse anything older
# VOWE_GRAPHIFY_DISABLE=1                        # switch it off entirely

# Semantic extraction of docs and schemas, which does need a key. Unset, Vowe
# runs `--code-only`: deterministic, local, and free.
# VOWE_GRAPHIFY_BACKEND=claude                   # claude | gemini | openai | ollama | ...
